{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H5Qrz7vRKzMDYT9nVKFUZu","type":"tool_result","content":"2:# _python-hook.sh — Python version resolver + hook invoker.\n5:# hook (check_agent_spawn.py, audit_log.py). Resolves `python3.12` →\n6:# `python3.11` → `python3.10` → `python3` and refuses anything below 3.9.\n10:# `python3` on a user's $PATH is not hermetic:\n17:# Letting Claude Code run `python3 ...` directly lets a mis-resolved PATH\n30:# `from __future__ import annotations` + `typing.Optional/Union` and\n36:#     \"command\": \"bash \\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\\\" check_agent_spawn.py\"\n45:# lack stdlib features (from __future__ import annotations, etc.).\n48:# entry, spawning a `python3 -c \"import sys...\"` subprocess every single\n61:  ver=$(python3 -c \"import sys; print(f\\\"{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}\\\")\" 2>/dev/null) || {\n62:    echo \"ERROR: python3 not found or invocable. Framework requires Python >=3.9.\" >&2\n80:# was forking an extra `python3 -c` subprocess per invocation. Removed\n83:# JSON-parse call INSIDE the existing per-invocation python3 spawn\n116:  \"python3.13\"\n117:  \"python3.12\"\n118:  \"python3.11\"\n119:  \"python3.10\"\n120:  \"python3.9\"\n121:  \"python3\"\n127:# `python3` exists, 5 `command -v` failures + 1 spawn of `python -c\n128:# \"import sys; print(...)\"` for version probe). Hot-path cost dominated\n134:# PATH changes (e.g. `brew install python@3.12`) so the freshest\n201:  # Emit \"MAJOR MINOR\" from `python --version` output (e.g. \"Python 3.12.3\")\n203:  \"$py\" -c 'import sys; print(sys.version_info[0], sys.version_info[1])' 2>/dev/null\n243:  # in the cache-miss branch. The gate's `python3 -c ...` spawn is ~15-20ms\n281:[_python-hook.sh] ERROR: No Python >= ${MIN_MAJOR}.${MIN_MINOR} found.\n284:  macOS:   brew install python@3.12\n285:  Ubuntu:  sudo apt install python3.12\n286:  Fedora:  sudo dnf install python3.12\n299:  echo \"[_python-hook.sh] ERROR: missing hook script name\" >&2\n308:  echo \"[_python-hook.sh] ERROR: hook not found: $HOOK_SCRIPT\" >&2\n322:# wrote stdout and the shim `exec`'d the hook, so the hook's own exit 0\n385:# path preserves the historical exec byte-for-byte (Claude/Codex unchanged).\n414:  # shim), or a passive grok event: preserve the historical exec (zero added\n416:  exec \"$FOUND_PY\" \"$HOOK_SCRIPT\" \"$@\"\n490:import json, sys\n528:          printf '%s\\n' '{\"decision\": \"deny\", \"reason\": \"hook emitted an unparseable deny-bearing payload; blocked fail-CLOSED by _python-hook.sh (original payload on stderr)\"}'"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2528d9c1-8eb1-455d-9821-50eb46f8d21a","uuid":"db531d1b-a9fa-42b8-91b3-3f897fe97cb5","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:56:51.047Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"2:# _python-hook.sh — Python version resolver + hook invoker.\n5:# hook (check_agent_spawn.py, audit_log.py). Resolves `python3.12` →\n6:# `python3.11` → `python3.10` → `python3` and refuses anything below 3.9.\n10:# `python3` on a user's $PATH is not hermetic:\n17:# Letting Claude Code run `python3 ...` directly lets a mis-resolved PATH\n30:# `from __future__ import annotations` + `typing.Optional/Union` and\n36:#     \"command\": \"bash \\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/_python-hook.sh\\\" check_agent_spawn.py\"\n45:# lack stdlib features (from __future__ import annotations, etc.).\n48:# entry, spawning a `python3 -c \"import sys...\"` subprocess every single\n61:  ver=$(python3 -c \"import sys; print(f\\\"{sys.version_info.major}.{sys.version_info.minor}\\\")\" 2>/dev/null) || {\n62:    echo \"ERROR: python3 not found or invocable. Framework requires Python >=3.9.\" >&2\n80:# was forking an extra `python3 -c` subprocess per invocation. Removed\n83:# JSON-parse call INSIDE the existing per-invocation python3 spawn\n116:  \"python3.13\"\n117:  \"python3.12\"\n118:  \"python3.11\"\n119:  \"python3.10\"\n120