e __main__. Library callers of decide() (mcp-server/handlers/spawn_agent.py:148, self_test.py) would then get a half-bound module and a NameError on every call instead of an import-time error. This can't happen today: the package __init__ imports both submodules before bind runs, and every __all__ name exists. Minimal fix: re-raise in the bind except block when __name__ != \"__main__\", matching _load_spawn_part.\n2. P2 — check_agent_spawn.py:39-47. The facade's imports of hashlib, unicodedata, re, os and Path now exist only so the rebound part functions can find them, and linters will flag them as unused. Removing them would fail silently. Without `hashlib`, _skill_ref_validate_hash_and_redact raises NameError, decide() raises, and main() allows, so SKILL REFERENCE hash validation stops working. Without `re`, _classify_file_assignment raises inside _enforce_spawn_rails's try, so the FILE ASSIGNMENT gate quietly returns None. Minimal fix: a bind-time check, or a test, that every co_names global of every bound function resolves in the facade namespace or builtins. Imports inside the part modules don't help, because the bound functions read the facade's globals.\n3. P2 — check_agent_spawn.py:600-602 says the REASON_* constants are \"at check_agent_spawn.py:188\"; they are now in _lib/agent_spawn/prompt_rules.py:93-106. check_agent_spawn.py:633 still calls the file \"this 1700-LoC file\". Fix the two references.\n4. P2 — check_agent_spawn.py:22-23, 50 and 642. These comments exist so .claude/scripts/gen-command-skill-hook-map.py, which derives guard involvement from literal mentions of `.claude/skills`/`SKILL.md` in registered hook source, keeps check_agent_spawn on the skill surface now that skill_reference.py lives under _lib/. The claim is fair (the bound helpers do validate SKILL.md references, and docs/COMMAND-SKILL-HOOK-MAP.md says its rule over-approximates). But the map row now rests on a comment, and deleting it drops the row silently. Fix: let the scanner follow a facade's _lib/<pkg> parts, or document the anchor.\n5. P2 (existed before this delta, not a regression) — kernel _lib/audit_emit.py:38 imports _lib/spool_writer.py, which is not kernel, and spool_writer.py:588 now hands off to _lib/_spool_writer_parts/, also not kernel. Both stay at the canonical/sentinel tier (_lib/**/*.py in canonical_edit/guards.py:34), exactly like spool_writer.py in v1.4.2. test_kernel_decomposition_coverage only follows imports out of kernel sources, so it can't see this hop. Follow-up: decide on purpose whether the audit spool writer belongs in _KERNEL_PATHS.","decision":"GO","sentence":"Both declared conditions this payload touches (5 and 7) hold against the code, the check_agent_spawn split moves the code without changing behavior or fail direction, and nothing at P0 or P1 was found, only P2 follow-ups."}}}
